  "final_text": "**Disposition:** CLOSE_FP (proposed). Confidence is 0.8. A human analyst makes the final decision.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The large BUY ICEBERG (O-00030261, 21,768 shares, 8.97x depth) was working. 5,835 shares (26.8%) executed before the only opposite-side trade, and that is more than the 544 sold. That supports genuine execution, so the trader intended the order to execute.\n2. The only opposite-side trade was a 544 SELL under a different parent order (C-T-X1005-05-B). The trader is an agency desk, so that is a different client's order, not a round trip against the iceberg. The iceberg's size was hidden, so it could not have signalled to move the price. Feature (b), a benefit from the opposite-side trade, is not established.\n3. There is no market event, risk event or repetition (`repetitions_in_session` is 1), and the trader has no prior alerts in 90 days. The remaining 15,933 shares were cancelled 2s after the SELL.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the SELL and the iceberg were the same client's order, or a repeat of the pattern on other days.",
